WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.169
♪♪

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.205
Hey, everybody.
Welcome back to "Corrections."

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.942
And let's get started.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:13.846
I said there were no direct
flights from LaGuardia to LAX.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.415
There is one.
There is one a week.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:19.319
Do you want to guess what
airline it is, Shoemaker?

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.220
Spirit Airlines.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.789
It's a true story.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:27.926
Spirit Airlines has
a Saturday morning flight

00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:29.928
from LaGuardia to LAX.

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:35.234
There's a rule at LaGuardia that
you cannot fly a flight

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:40.039
that's more than 1,500 miles
outside LaGuardia airport,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.909
but that rule
is waived on Saturdays.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:47.279
So Spirit Airlines
took advantage of it.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.515
And, you know, if you're going
from New York to L.A.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.851
and you want to see the stars,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.553
they're probably not
on that flight.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.588
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.493
Someone from Spirit Airlines

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.195
actually reached out
to tell us that.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.197
They didn't reach out directly.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.367
They had to connect in Florida.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.402
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:18.911
We talked about people taking
horse pills, ivermectin.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.980
Horse pills -- We said,
"Don't take horse pills

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.016
to treat COVID."

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.552
And a lot of people said,
"Look, you know,

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:29.188
the prescription ivermecshin --
ivermectin, excuse me,

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.356
is a pill.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:35.528
The horse medicine ivermectin
is a paste.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.631
So we should have said --
We were wrong to say,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.400
"Don't eat horse pills.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.905
What we should have said is,
"Don't eat horse paste."

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.341
So I guess we're the dummies.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:53.546
In the back -- I think --
You know, and, again,

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.748
like, don't eat paste
in general.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.751
If we learned anything
in kindergarten

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.487
that we could take with us
the rest of our life,

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.323
don't eat the paste.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.127
We've talked about
the knitting community,

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.197
the foul-mouthed,
short-tempered,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.800
incredibly diverse
knitting community.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.703
And as a little
Easter egg for them,

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.237
on the back of my card
last week, I wrote,

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.507
"Knit one, purl two,
relax three."

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.744
I spelled purl "P-E-A-R-L."

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.479
So, once again,
they did what they --

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:30.383
Their natural state is outrage.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.020
They said, "It's not --
You spelled it wrong.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.255
It's P-U-R-L."

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.722
But that's not what I was doing.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:40.660
I was saying,
"One, knitters, listen up.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:45.364
Two, here is
a pearl of wisdom...

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.567
which is, three, relax."

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.673
Oh, this is bad.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:03:00.346
I talked about Twiki the Robot,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.249
said he was from
"Battlestar Galactica."

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.751
He's from "Buck Rogers."

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.986
And a lot of you said that
I did that on purpose.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:11.690
I was, you know,
throwing out jackal bait.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:16.596
I would -- First of all,
I would never do that --

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:20.633
I would never do that
for this, okay?

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:24.170
Because there was
a real cost when I did that.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.506
I had my nerd card revoked.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:28.741
And that's not just,
like, a thing.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.945
That's a real thing
you have and you need.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:35.948
Like, my nerd card has come in
super-handy, even recently.

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:41.353
I got to get the vaccine early,
because a nerd card --

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:43.288
When you have a nerd card,

00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:46.692
they just assume you
have moderate-to-severe asthma.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.161
And, by the way, asthma
community, don't come at me,

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.663
thinking I'm making fun of
people with asthma.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.898
I got it.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.702
I still carry an inhaler, okay?

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:59.138
You want to come at me
about my asthma,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:02.341
you just name
the time and the place.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.811
Ideally a place
without ragweed...

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:08.147
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.249
...or pet dander.

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.385
You know what was really --
Patton Oswalt

00:04:13.385 --> 00:04:16.990
was the one who called me to say
my nerd card was revoked.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.925
So they had a friend do it.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.129
But I will say this about Twiki.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.531
A lot of people were like,
"You idiot.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:29.836
Twiki was from 'Buck Rogers.'"

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.069
I'm not lying --

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:34.340
there were seven different
spellings of Twiki.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.776
So you're not better than me.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:42.181
Couple people spelled it Twiggy,
with two G's.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:46.819
Twiggy, of course, was the...

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:53.159
robot in the short-lived sitcom
"Laverne &amp; Shirley in Space."

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.194
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.029 --> 00:05:01.267
Twiggy and Len --
Len Bot and Twiggy.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.670
where the robots --
they would...

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.772
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:10.676
They would show up at
the funniest time.

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:14.247
Laverne and Shirley --
they'd be on the space station.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.416
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.851
And Shirley would be like, "I
don't know about space, Laverne.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.586
There's the
creepiest creatures here."

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.488
[ Robotic voice ]
"Hello!"

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:32.765
Also, you know, I'll apologize
for getting wrong that Twiki

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:36.501
was from, you know,
"Buck Rogers" and not

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.870
"Battlestar," but you know
who else should apologize?

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:43.042
How about Buck Rogers for
thinking, in the 25th century,

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.644
this is what robots
would look like?

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.615
And we're barely into
the 21st century,

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:54.520
and, like, Boston Dynamics
has robots doing, like, parkour.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.757
And they were like, "The
25th century, they'll have,

00:05:57.757 --> 00:06:00.893
like, metal bowl cuts."

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.730
That's -- You know what
that actor is?

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.532
Gil Faizon.
"Charmed, I'm sure."

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.137
We've been talking about
"The New York Times"

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.306
spelling bee.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.674
This is not a correction,
but it was really sweet.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.643
The people over at
"The New York Times,"

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:20.679
the word-games people,
sent me a spelling-bee mug,

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.548
which I thought was very nice.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:27.253
And a card, which surprised me,

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.255
because I just thought they'd
have better...

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.256
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:32.625
...handwriting.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.162
I don't know.

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.763
That's, like, foolish to
assume that people, like,

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.666
good at word games
would have good penmanship,

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.936
but that's --
that's a shame on me.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:48.240
I finished the last corrections
by saying, "See you September."

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.709
And I was told by a
bunch of people,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.345
I don't see you, you see me.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:58.518
We had a graphic of an F Train

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:01.653
in a flooded 59th Street
subway station.

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:04.657
The F Train does not
stop at 59th Street.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:07.493
I said "one or two things"
last night,

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:11.063
when I meant to say
"one of two things.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:13.732
We talked about being taught
fractals in high school.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.034
A lot of people said
you don't get taught

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:16.235
fractals in high school.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.337
I also said it
would have been great if "AOC"

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.005
could have taught me math
in high school,

00:07:20.005 --> 00:07:24.476
and a bunch of people,
which I think was very cruel,

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:26.545
said she wasn't even born when
I was in high school.

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:28.981
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.417
But she was.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:35.488
When I was a sophomore,
she was born.

00:07:38.156 --> 00:07:41.594
A lot of --
I guess it's an old wives' tale.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.897
You can go swimming right
after you eat.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.265
You don't have to wait
30 minutes,

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:50.269
so just have a big old meal
and get right in the pool.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.472
This was a little hurtful.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.741
Someone said -- I guess --
You know, and, again,

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.376
not everybody has to like
"Corrections."

00:07:58.376 --> 00:08:00.412
It's not for everyone.

00:08:01.346 --> 00:08:04.850
Someone said, "How do I --"
This was a comment they left.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.585
"How do I opt out of these?"

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:08.621
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.058
So...

00:08:13.992 --> 00:08:18.730
So, the cursor --
If you move it, there's --

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:21.867
It's, like -- There's like
two lines like this.

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:23.902
And then if you click --
It's, like, a --

00:08:23.902 --> 00:08:25.171
Like, if you click it, it's --

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:28.474
It's, like, the universal
symbol for "pause."

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.609
You just hit it, and it stops.

00:08:30.609 --> 00:08:34.814
And then you just go about it,
doing something else.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:37.616
The film is called
"The Goonies,"

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:39.352
not "Goonies."

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:45.991
Also, it turns out,
a lot of movies were shot in

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:48.194
Astoria, Oregon,
where "The Goonies" is shot.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:52.265
"Short Circuit,"
"Kindergarten Cop,"

00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:55.134
"Teenage Mutant
Ninja Turtles III,"

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.069
"Ring Two."

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.205
Not bad.

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:02.274
My question to those of you
in Astoria --

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:05.644
do you have film tourism?

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:10.515
Do people who like those films
come to look around?

00:09:10.515 --> 00:09:13.052
You know,
at the Astoria Airport,

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:17.089
which is in Warrenton --
shame on you --

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:22.161
can you buy a
"It's not a tumor" shirt?

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:24.196
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:30.502
Or a "Number 5 is alive"
coffee mug.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.304
It was just a question.

00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:34.373
That's not a correction.

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:40.513
Talked about --
speaking of "The Goonies" --

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:43.915
the importance to remember,
when you're doing impressions,

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:46.052
don't do Sloth.

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:48.187
Sloth was a character
in "The Goonies."

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:50.956
And just don't do Sloth.

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:53.892
It's a hard -- A lot
of comedians who had, like,

00:09:53.892 --> 00:09:58.297
big Sloth chunks
in their act complain now,

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:00.799
'cause they're
like, "I can't do Sloth."

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:02.968
And a lot of them,
like, that's their act now.

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:04.803
It's like,
"You can't do Sloth anymore."

00:10:04.803 --> 00:10:07.539
But then a lot of them
still do Sloth.

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:10.810
I'm like, "Which is it?"

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.244
You know?

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:15.114
Can't have your Baby Ruth
and eat it, too.

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:20.453
Anyway, I talked about how
"Don't do Sloth"

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:25.624
is the motto of Impression Camp.

00:10:25.624 --> 00:10:26.892
But it's in Latin.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:30.262
I couldn't remember
the exact Latin of the seal

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:33.365
at Impression Camp,
but I wanted to get it right,

00:10:33.365 --> 00:10:35.267
so I went to one of
our producers, Emily,

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:37.169
because we actually use
a translation service

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:39.104
whenever we do something
in a foreign language.

00:10:39.104 --> 00:10:42.808
And I said, "Can you find out,
using the translation service,

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:45.044
how you would say,
'Don't do Sloth' in Latin?"

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:47.313
And she came back to me
and she showed me

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:49.281
the e-mail from
the translation service.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:52.484
And they said,
"As you likely know --"

00:10:52.484 --> 00:10:54.019
Seemed a little
passive-aggressive

00:10:54.019 --> 00:10:55.588
right off the bat.

00:10:56.956 --> 00:11:00.592
"As you likely know,
Latin is a dead language.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:05.164
So we're not gonna be able to
get you an answer today."

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:07.066
You know, 'cause they said
they usually go to --

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:08.667
You know what kind --
What two professions

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:12.137
do you think they go to,
Shoemaker, to get Latin?

00:11:12.137 --> 00:11:15.307
-Medical?
-Doctors. Correct.

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:17.275
-Legal.
-Priests.

00:11:17.275 --> 00:11:19.745
-Oh!
-And I get it.

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:22.147
You don't want to, like --
They also said

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:24.082
they're notoriously
hard to get in touch with,

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:25.384
doctors and priests.

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:28.787
And I -- You wouldn't want to
interrupt a surgery

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:31.557
to find out how to say,
"Don't do Sloth."

00:11:32.758 --> 00:11:35.460
"Doctor, stop what you're doing.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.929
It's for
'Late Night with Seth Meyers.'

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:38.497
No, no, not broadcast."

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:40.533
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.936 --> 00:11:48.407
Anyway, so, we couldn't get
it from the translation service,

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:49.941
and so I had to go to
Google Translate.

00:11:49.941 --> 00:11:51.877
And, guys, look,
when you go to Google Translate,

00:11:51.877 --> 00:11:53.545
you've already lost.

00:11:53.545 --> 00:11:55.381
It's already too late.

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:57.182
You're not gonna get
what you need going --

00:11:57.182 --> 00:11:58.951
Google -- It's like when you --
It's like if

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:00.586
you want a picture taken of
you and your friends,

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:04.023
and the only person you
can find is a very old woman.

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:06.925
She'll take the picture, but
you're never gonna look at it.

00:12:06.925 --> 00:12:11.763
So, I used Google Translate for
"Don't do Sloth."

00:12:11.763 --> 00:12:14.132
And here's what someone
told me it translated to,

00:12:14.132 --> 00:12:18.137
'cause, you know, of course,
the jackals all speak Latin.

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.607
"Do not make of the wild meat
for the para--"

00:12:22.607 --> 00:12:24.075
[ Laughs ]

00:12:24.075 --> 00:12:26.211
"Do not meek -"

00:12:26.211 --> 00:12:29.848
"Do not make of the wild meat
for the paralysis."

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:31.650
"Don't do Sloth."

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:35.921
A lot of you have also
noted that when I

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:37.622
first mentioned Impression Camp
on this show,

00:12:37.622 --> 00:12:38.957
I said it was a place
I went where they would

00:12:38.957 --> 00:12:41.460
stop getting me
to do impressions,

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.595
but I've since
reframed as a place

00:12:43.595 --> 00:12:46.165
where they've helped me
hone my impressions.

00:12:46.165 --> 00:12:47.966
So, what happened was this.

00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:50.536
I did originally go so that
I could stop

00:12:50.536 --> 00:12:56.074
doing impressions, but then they
heard me do my impressions

00:12:56.074 --> 00:12:59.078
and they said I have the gift.

00:12:59.078 --> 00:13:01.446
[ Laughter ]

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:04.716
So they moved me from
Impression Camp to

00:13:04.716 --> 00:13:07.319
Impression Academy.

00:13:09.721 --> 00:13:13.258
And the dean of
Impression Academy --

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:15.661
a little guy, Rich...

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:17.696
[ Laughter ]

00:13:20.632 --> 00:13:24.169
he came over
and he said, "Well --"

00:13:24.169 --> 00:13:27.106
He always...

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:28.507
He would always start, "Well..."

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:30.009
I think...
[ Laughter ]

00:13:30.009 --> 00:13:32.811
I think that's how he
gets into Reagan.

00:13:32.811 --> 00:13:35.247
He goes,
"Well, you've got the gift."

00:13:38.383 --> 00:13:40.386
God, what else?

